# Trivy ignore file — acknowledged CVEs for the Trivy scans.
#
# Add a CVE ID on its own line, each with a justification comment above it.
# Entries here suppress findings in the filesystem and image scans of
# security.yml and in the "Snapshot build" scan.
# Keep this list short and review it regularly.
#
# Example:
#   # CVE-0000-00000 — false positive: package not reachable at runtime.
#   CVE-0000-00000

# CVE-2026-40345 — deepmerge-ts: stack exhaustion when merging recursive object graphs.
# deepmerge-ts 7.1.5 is in the tree only as a dependency of @prisma/config,
# which the Prisma CLI uses to merge its own configuration when the migration
# job starts. The API never loads it, and the CLI merges prisma.config.ts from
# this repository, not anything a user sends.
# No fix is installable: every Prisma 7 release pins 7.1.5 exactly and the
# patched line starts at 8.0.0.
# Remove when Prisma ships a patched deepmerge-ts.
# Justification mirrored in .github/scripts/audit-allowlist.json (GHSA-ggr8-5vv4-36mx).
CVE-2026-40345
